% n14: an inductive whose constructor does NOT return the type being declared.
% `Foo : Sort 0 | bad : Sort 0` -- `bad` builds a Sort, not a Foo, so it is not
% a constructor of Foo at all. Added because mutation testing showed the
% constructor-return rule was untested: removing it broke nothing.
1 sort 0
2 sort 0
inductive Foo : 1 | bad : 2
